  "helpTitle": "Help & legal",
  "helpAsOf": "As of 2026",
  "helpLegalBody": "The app is only a player and contains no channels. You add an M3U link or an Xtream login from a source you have the right to use. Free legal sources: the public iptv-org playlists (links published by the broadcasters themselves; some stop working or are geo-blocked), or your own satellite receiver if it can export M3U. Free official apps: Aloula, Shahid's free tier and Thmanyah. Legal paid subscriptions (Shahid VIP, TOD by beIN, stc tv, OSN+) work only in their official apps and don't give you an M3U link or Xtream login. Beware of cheap “IPTV subscriptions” sold on WhatsApp and Telegram: they are usually unlicensed, the new Saudi Copyright Law (in force since August 2026) raises the penalties, and they carry a real risk of fraud and malware.",
  "helpWarningSignsTitle": "Signs of an unlicensed seller",
  "helpWarningSigns": "• Thousands of premium channels for a small yearly fee\n• Sold through WhatsApp, Telegram or social media ads\n• An Xtream code or M3U link instead of an official app\n• No commercial registration and no VAT invoice",
